WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.135
-Polls continue to show that
Americans overwhelmingly support

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:04.537
the Black Lives Matter protests

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.639
against police brutality
and systemic racism,

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.876
and that's why the President
and the police are lashing out.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.812
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:16.082
♪♪

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.484
We're living through a moment
of national crisis

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:20.687
unprecedented in our lifetimes.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.521
The nation
is convulsing with outrage

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:24.290
over the brutal murder
of George Floyd,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.493
local police
and federal law enforcement

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.028
have responded to
peaceful protests with violence,

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:32.899
there are secret police
with no name badges or insignia

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.534
lined up in the nation's capital

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.237
like extras from a [bleep]
Steven Seagal movie --

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.571
not one of the high-enders.
One of the...

00:00:39.571 --> 00:00:41.807
A highly infectious virus

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:43.976
which has killed
over 110,000 Americans

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:45.278
hasn't gone anywhere.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.246
I mean, we're learning more
about COVID-19 every day,

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:48.848
but I doubt we'll ever find out

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.017
it's prone
to politely excuse itself.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.886
"Hey, we didn't realize

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.454
the extent of this
whole racism thing

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.356
you have going on,
so we're just gonna...

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:58.758
We're just gonna go."

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.460
Unemployment is at
its highest level

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.727
since the Great Depression.

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:03.896
If this was the first chapter
of a YA novel,

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:06.632
the teen protagonist would say
"screw it" and move to Canada.

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:09.369
And through it all,
the President is a recluse

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.770
cowering in a bunker
behind an 8-foot-tall fence

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.272
like JD Scowlinger.
[Salinger]

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:15.074
Next time he appears in public,
he's going to have

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.677
10-inch fingernails
and a Unabomber beard.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:20.846
Of course, his beard
would probably look like this.

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:24.316
Yeah, it's a hair joke. Sue me.

00:01:24.316 --> 00:01:26.886
Just think of it as a way of
taking a breath of clean air

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.855
before diving back
into [Bleep] River.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.557
This is a moment of
national anguish, heartache,

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:34.326
and suffering unlike any
we've seen in recent memory.

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:36.262
Or, as the President
put it on Friday...

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.830
-Today is probably,
if you think of it,

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.465
the greatest comeback
in American history.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.033
But you --
It's not going to stop here.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.935
It's going to keep going.

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:44.437
-Jesus.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:47.140
I haven't heard anything that
tone-deaf since Rob Gronkowski

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.440
appeared on "The Masked Singer."

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.242
I mean, I'm still --
I'm still pretty impressed

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:52.045
they found a mascot head
big enough

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.312
to fit over his actual head.

00:01:53.312 --> 00:01:54.646
I always assumed Rob Gronkowski

00:01:54.646 --> 00:01:57.550
was a "Masked Singer" costume
with a singer inside him,

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.686
that one of the greatest
tight ends of all time

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.455
was actually Patti LaBelle
in a Gronkowski suit.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:05.859
But this isn't a comeback yet.
It's not a comeback at all.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.260
When the Knicks are losing by 30

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.362
and hit a 3-pointer
at the buzzer to lose by 27,

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.363
the deejay doesn't play
"Y'all Ready For This?"

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:12.665
There's no question

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.735
the May jobs report was good
and better than expected.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.670
And also a little misleading.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.940
I mean, a lot of the jobs that
were supposedly created are jobs

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.576
that were lost to the pandemic
being re-created.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:26.012
It's like bragging
that you lost 3 pounds

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.580
right after you gained
45 pounds.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.949
But to suggest
that we're not mired

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.619
in an unprecedented calamity
is just deranged.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:36.388
Nearly 40% of households with
incomes of less than $40,000

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:37.757
have reported job losses.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.725
Meanwhile, U.S. billionaires

00:02:39.725 --> 00:02:43.729
have become $565 billion richer
since March 18th.

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:45.998
That's right --
billionaires actually

00:02:45.998 --> 00:02:47.867
got richer during the pandemic,

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.969
while the poorest households
lost jobs.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.370
We're living in a dystopian film

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.005
written and directed
by Bernie Sanders.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:54.707
"See it, don't see it,
who cares?

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.910
But one thing we all agree on --
$6 for popcorn is insane!"

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.013
I miss him being around because
I think it became a passable --

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.448
a passable impression.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.350
But, of course,
Trump is celebrating because

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.787
things really have been just
fine for his wealthy patrons

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.688
and the corporate husks
he chums around with

00:03:09.688 --> 00:03:10.990
at the Mar-a-Lago omelette bar,

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.692
which, knowing Trump,
is probably BYO eggs.

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:15.094
"We provide the peppers.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.863
The pepper? We just have
the one pepper, but don't worry.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.998
It's a good pepper.
It's like a red or a green.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.801
It's -- It's a yellow?
We have one yellow pepper

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:25.237
for everyone at
the omelette station to share."

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:27.373
And while millions of Americans
have been in the streets

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:30.242
protesting systemic racism
and police brutality

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:32.945
only to be met with
more brutality from the police

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:35.882
and a pandemic that has killed
110,000 Americans

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.084
and unemployment
is at the highest point

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:39.519
since the Great Depression,

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.921
Trump is still bragging
about the stock market.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.723
-Our stock market is almost --

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:46.225
It's just short
of an all-time high.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:51.130
I've had 144 all-time-high
stock markets

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.898
during a three-and-a-half-year
period.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:54.500
Nobody's ever
come close to that.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.469
And we're going to do it again.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.604
But it's going to be
even stronger than last time.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.373
When I would say that to you
two, three months ago,

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.008
I could see what's happen --
I have a good f--

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.309
I've always done well
with numbers.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:06.011
-No, you haven't always
done well with numbers.

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:08.147
I mean,
just ask these two zeros.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:10.650
No one who is actually good
with numbers ever has to say,

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.384
"I've always done well
with numbers."

00:04:12.384 --> 00:04:14.954
If your doctor took your
blood pressure and then said,

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.823
"I've always done well
with numbers,"

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:19.125
you might want to get
a second opinion.

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.993
"Yeah, my last doctor
said my blood pressure

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:24.864
was, uh...
negative-52 degrees Celsius.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.366
Is that -- Is that bad?"

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.267
But the more shocking thing

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.536
is Trump bragging
about the stock market.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.038
If 40 million people
have filed for unemployment

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:35.274
and over 100,000 have died

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.910
and police are violently beating
peaceful protesters,

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.413
maybe the stock market
hitting an all-time high

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.481
doesn't actually mean
we as a country

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:44.383
are at an all-time high.

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:47.219
We used to hear that the stock
market hates uncertainty,

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:49.956
and I don't know
what clearer sign of uncertainty

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.657
there could possibly be

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:54.060
than unemployed Americans
putting on industrial masks

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.361
and stepping over
empty tear-gas containers

00:04:56.361 --> 00:04:58.664
on their way to cash
a $1,200 government check.

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:00.966
Maybe -- Maybe this is your hint
that the stock market

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.102
is actually bull [bleep].
Kind of like when you're a kid

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.037
and you find the Christmas
presents in the closet,

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:06.438
and your first thought is,
"That's weird.

00:05:06.438 --> 00:05:09.208
Why would Santa store
his presents in our closet?"

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:12.111
Then your mom signs a permission
slip for a field trip,

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.346
and you think, "That is weird.
Why does Santa

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:15.948
have the same handwriting
as my mom?"

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.883
And then you come downstairs
early on Christmas

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:20.452
and see your dad on the floor
using all the curse words

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:22.989
as he tries to tie a bow
around a Hatchimal,

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:26.525
and you finally realize,
"Oh, Mom and Dad work for Santa,

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:28.627
and I'm Santa's baby."

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:30.963
Trump and his allies
have been gleefully celebrating

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:33.365
one good jobs report amid
an ongoing national calamity

00:05:33.365 --> 00:05:35.468
to the point where
you can't help but conclude

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:38.303
that they are totally detached
from reality.

00:05:38.303 --> 00:05:40.172
Watch this very real clip

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:42.007
the White House posted
over the weekend

00:05:42.007 --> 00:05:45.177
from Trump's top economic
advisor, Larry Kudlow.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:46.812
-America is coming back.

00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:51.450
Three million new jobs,
lower unemployment rate,

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:55.387
furloughed temporary layoffs
going back to work.

00:05:55.387 --> 00:05:58.123
Green shoots
popping up everywhere.

00:05:58.123 --> 00:06:00.259
Stocks are soaring.

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:02.528
POTUS policies are working.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:06.565
Stay with the winners!
Trump and Pence and me!

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:09.234
The best is yet to come!

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:11.504
-Are you about to
sell me a mattress?

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:14.473
Are you telling me to
"come on down to America"?

00:06:14.473 --> 00:06:16.241
I feel like I'm watching
a local commercial

00:06:16.241 --> 00:06:19.111
for Crazy Larry Kudlow's
Discount Furniture Warehouse.

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:22.448
"Come on down to Larry
Discount Furniture Warehouse!

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:25.918
Our quality is Kud-high,
but our prices are Kud-low!"

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:31.290
"You want another take, Larry?"
"No, yeah, we got it!"

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.859
Of course, Trump and his buddies
are gleefully celebrating

00:06:33.859 --> 00:06:35.361
the soaring stock market.

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:38.163
Our deeply unjust system
works for them just fine,

00:06:38.163 --> 00:06:40.733
inflating the wealth of the most
privileged people in our society

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.969
even in a time
of abject misery and crisis

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:44.970
while crushing
the poor and working class.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.506
It's rigged to protect
the privileged and the powerful,

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:49.074
and the same
is true of policing.

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:51.176
Last week, you might remember
Trump had this to say

00:06:51.176 --> 00:06:53.045
when he gave a speech
threatening to unleash

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:56.315
America's military
against American citizens.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:07:00.319
-One law and order.

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.054
And that is what it is.

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:05.691
One law.
We have one beautiful law.

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.660
-Okay, first of all,
I don't know why you need

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.261
to be creepy toward "the law."

00:07:09.261 --> 00:07:10.996
"Beautiful law"
sounds like a show on USA

00:07:10.996 --> 00:07:13.499
about a group of swimsuit models
who become public defenders.

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:16.068
"We, the jury,
find the defendant sexy."

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:19.771
Second, it's not true.
There isn't "one law and order."

00:07:19.771 --> 00:07:22.375
We know that because anyone
who did even a fraction

00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:24.543
of what you have done
would be in jail by now,

00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:26.045
never mind the serial tax fraud

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:27.947
or profiting
from your public office

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:29.948
or the 10 allegations
of obstruction of justice

00:07:29.948 --> 00:07:31.450
in the Mueller report.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.753
Prosecutors have already
named you in an indictment

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:36.055
as the guy who orchestrated
a criminal scheme

00:07:36.055 --> 00:07:39.191
to pay hush money during an
election to cover up an affair.

00:07:39.191 --> 00:07:41.193
We have the check
with your signature on it.

00:07:41.193 --> 00:07:43.662
You literally signed
the evidence.

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:45.798
Even O.J. knew better
than to make it clear

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.900
the Ford Bronco was his.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.702
There isn't one law and order.

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:51.737
There are two separate
and distinct systems.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:54.740
One is a system where the law
serves people of privilege,

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.408
and order preserves
their privilege,

00:07:56.408 --> 00:07:57.876
where the police work for them.

00:07:57.876 --> 00:08:00.679
And the other is a racist system
of predatory policing

00:08:00.679 --> 00:08:03.382
that systematically devalues
black lives

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:06.785
and which acts as an occupying
force in their own communities.

00:08:06.785 --> 00:08:09.855
And now we're seeing that system
unleashed on mass demonstrations

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:12.391
across the country,
with one video after another

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:14.192
making the rounds
of police descending

00:08:14.192 --> 00:08:15.561
on peaceful protesters

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:17.530
and subjecting them
to brutal violence,

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.465
including here in new York.

00:08:19.465 --> 00:08:22.534
-Last night in New York City,
there was both a curfew

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:24.236
and also a large
peaceful protest

00:08:24.236 --> 00:08:26.538
that was happening
after the curfew.

00:08:26.538 --> 00:08:28.474
The peaceful protest
then descended into violence,

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:30.676
not because of the protesters,

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:35.014
but because the NYPD
started beating people.

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:37.082
This is what that moment
looked like.

00:08:37.082 --> 00:08:38.985
This is footage shot
in Manhattan last night.

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:40.987
It appears to show NYPD officers

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:42.821
just striking
a person on a bicycle

00:08:42.821 --> 00:08:44.924
as onlookers recorded the scene
while stuck in traffic.

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:47.659
They are aghast, by the way.
And then other officers joined.

00:08:47.659 --> 00:08:50.562
So there's four people beating
this one guy on his bike?

00:08:50.562 --> 00:08:52.598
Videos have been appearing
on Twitter from protests

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:54.033
in New York City
of the past week,

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:56.868
showing police using batons
on protesters.

00:08:56.868 --> 00:08:58.603
-What the [bleep] is going on?!

00:08:58.603 --> 00:09:00.939
Four cops beating a guy
walking away with his bike?

00:09:00.939 --> 00:09:02.474
That's never called for.

00:09:02.474 --> 00:09:05.377
Even if he's one of those bikers
who overuses his bell,

00:09:05.377 --> 00:09:09.081
the most -- the absolutely most
they deserve is a middle finger.

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:10.783
These aren't just
some isolated scuffles.

00:09:10.783 --> 00:09:12.284
We're seeing it
across the country.

00:09:12.284 --> 00:09:13.718
They're trying
to send a message.

00:09:13.718 --> 00:09:15.220
That's why they're raining
tear gas

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.423
and flashbangs and pepper spray

00:09:17.423 --> 00:09:20.125
down on everyone
from protesters to reporters.

00:09:20.125 --> 00:09:23.695
Like this cop just casually
launching pepper balls

00:09:23.695 --> 00:09:26.732
at a reporter who's reporting
it live on the local news.

00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:28.233
Think of how shameless
you have to be

00:09:28.233 --> 00:09:29.568
to do that on live television.

00:09:29.568 --> 00:09:31.370
What's that cop
going to do next?

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.606
Live-stream himself
knocking over a liquor store

00:09:33.606 --> 00:09:35.741
or parking
in a handicapped spot?

00:09:35.741 --> 00:09:38.044
Police are lashing out
aggressively

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:40.179
because they see
that the protests are working

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:42.414
and that there's a growing
demand for police accountability

00:09:42.414 --> 00:09:45.551
and for police resources
to be shifted elsewhere.

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:47.052
The mass demonstrations

00:09:47.052 --> 00:09:49.387
have had a powerful impact
on public opinion.

00:09:49.387 --> 00:09:51.590
A new poll found that Americans
support the protests

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:54.660
sparked by the death of George
Floyd by a nearly 2-to-1 margin.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.595
By a 27-percentage-point margin,

00:09:56.595 --> 00:09:58.464
Americans agree that blacks
and other minorities

00:09:58.464 --> 00:09:59.931
are not treated equally
with whites

00:09:59.931 --> 00:10:01.867
by the criminal justice system.

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:03.802
And that is huge. Huge.

00:10:03.802 --> 00:10:05.871
I mean, you have to remember
millions of people --

00:10:05.871 --> 00:10:07.406
most of them
over the age of 90 --

00:10:07.406 --> 00:10:09.007
see this [bleep] every night.

00:10:09.007 --> 00:10:12.244
-Big companies, cynical,
soulless, craven corporations

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:15.715
like Pepsi, Intel, and Airbnb,
are funding this chaos.

00:10:15.715 --> 00:10:17.816
They're giving money
to Black Lives Matter,

00:10:17.816 --> 00:10:20.019
which is pushing
to defund the police.

00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:22.121
But it isn't just
major corporations

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:23.154
that are fueling all of this.

00:10:23.154 --> 00:10:24.623
Celebrities are, too,

00:10:24.623 --> 00:10:26.758
by paying to get
violent rioters out of jail.

00:10:26.758 --> 00:10:29.028
As you read through this --
we're going to scroll

00:10:29.028 --> 00:10:31.096
through their names
on the right side of the screen.

00:10:31.096 --> 00:10:33.032
First off, actor Steve Carell
from "The Office"

00:10:33.032 --> 00:10:35.201
donated to
the Minnesota Freedom Fund,

00:10:35.201 --> 00:10:37.235
which is providing bail
to rioters.

00:10:37.235 --> 00:10:41.173
Seth Rogen, Don Cheadle,
Janelle Monáe donated, as well.

00:10:41.173 --> 00:10:42.674
The cast of
"Brooklyn Nine-Nine,"

00:10:42.674 --> 00:10:45.477
a police comedy, gave 100 grand
to help bail out people

00:10:45.477 --> 00:10:49.447
who may very well have attacked
those they portray on TV.

00:10:49.447 --> 00:10:51.850
Hollywood power couple
Blake Lively and Ryan Reynolds

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:55.954
donated $200,000
to the NAACP Legal Defense Fund.

00:10:55.954 --> 00:10:57.389
-Wow, Tucker! You got 'em.

00:10:57.389 --> 00:10:59.392
Steve Carell's career
will never be the same

00:10:59.392 --> 00:11:01.260
now that you included him
in your little

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.995
fifth-grade
PowerPoint presentation.

00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:05.330
I'm surprised you didn't
throw in some '90s clip art

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:07.065
like a globe or a cat.

00:11:07.065 --> 00:11:08.567
Seriously,
why are your graphics so bad?

00:11:08.567 --> 00:11:11.770
This looks like a 12-year-old's
Geocities website.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:14.673
Couldn't even spell
Chrissy Teigen's name right.

00:11:14.673 --> 00:11:17.276
I mean, I'm doing my show
from the attic,

00:11:17.276 --> 00:11:18.543
but we can still pull together

00:11:18.543 --> 00:11:20.145
a halfway
decent-looking graphic.

00:11:20.145 --> 00:11:21.847
For example,
here is Tucker Carlson

00:11:21.847 --> 00:11:23.248
with his pants around his ankles

00:11:23.248 --> 00:11:25.351
being carried away
by a huge bird.

00:11:25.351 --> 00:11:29.020
Ah! Nope. Never mind.
We also have a typo.

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:30.556
I take it back. [Bleep] Tucker.

00:11:30.556 --> 00:11:33.793
This stuff is, uh, hard.
It's hard to do.

00:11:33.793 --> 00:11:35.260
The privileged and the powerful,

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:37.362
the people served by a racist
system of predatory policing,

00:11:37.362 --> 00:11:39.832
see that the public
overwhelmingly supports

00:11:39.832 --> 00:11:41.834
the protests, and that's why
they're lashing out.

00:11:41.834 --> 00:11:44.570
In recent days, the protests
have only continued to swell,

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:46.238
with massive peaceful crowds

00:11:46.238 --> 00:11:48.006
streaming into cities
across the country.

00:11:48.006 --> 00:11:50.443
If lawmakers can learn anything
from these crowds,

00:11:50.443 --> 00:11:52.744
it's that mild reforms
won't cut it.

00:11:52.744 --> 00:11:54.813
As we've seen, police will abuse
their authority

00:11:54.813 --> 00:11:56.182
under any circumstances.

00:11:56.182 --> 00:11:58.216
It's a fundamentally
corrupt system.

00:11:58.216 --> 00:12:00.819
That's why you're hearing
protesters embrace the refrain

00:12:00.819 --> 00:12:02.187
to defund the police.

00:12:02.187 --> 00:12:03.989
We need to shift the money
we're spending on tanks

00:12:03.989 --> 00:12:06.992
and tear gas and batons and
move it to community programs

00:12:06.992 --> 00:12:09.094
like housing assistance
and health care.

00:12:09.094 --> 00:12:10.662
It's not hard to do the math.

00:12:10.662 --> 00:12:12.230
Just put someone in charge
who's...

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:13.732
-Always done well with numbers.

00:12:13.732 --> 00:12:15.334
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:15.334 --> 00:12:18.237
♪♪

00:12:18.237 --> 00:12:20.372 line:0%
As New York struggles
to reopen this week,

00:12:20.372 --> 00:12:22.207 line:0%
remember that we are still
a city in crisis,

00:12:22.207 --> 00:12:23.909 line:0%
and City Harvest
has been stepping up

00:12:23.909 --> 00:12:25.377 line:0%
to meet the increased need.

00:12:25.377 --> 00:12:27.779 line:0%
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the "donate" button.

00:12:27.779 --> 00:12:30.750 line:0%
Stay safe. Wash your hands.
We love you.

